WEBVTT

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.740
Hundreds ago, these woods were the site of a busy supply depot for the Union Army.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.430
Food, ammunition, medicine were all brought in by trains,

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.330
sent ahead by men and wagons to the front lines,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.720
far removed from the field of battle.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.840
And there was little occasion for the usual...

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:38.070
heroics of war, loyalty, bravery, sacrifice. There was little occasion, too, for a man to think about

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:47.630
death once, when death came to claim a victim under, shall we say, unusual circumstances. It

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:58.760
all began in 1862. Spring night, a fettered soldier named Jess Bradley

